Z||000003||FieroLisa||01-13-2001||02:47 PM||||Happened to me this summer. I had a new detachable face Panasonic CD player and I put the face in the center console glove box thingie. So whoever the @ss was that stole it, must have looked for the face first. When you get a detachable face one, actually take the face with you every time you get out of the car, a thief would be a lot less likely to steal it that way. I also had my amp, subs, radar detector and neons stolen too. $1,100 worth of stuff.<BR>I was thinking about getting an alarm, but a good thief knows how to cut those wires so fast you would barely know it was going off. Anyway in parking lots, people are so used to hearing alarms tripped, they barely pay attention anymore.<BR>Sorry about your luck though!!!!!!<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
