Z||000005||Joe4x4||01-13-2001||03:46 PM||||Sorry to hear that,...it too happened to me last year. Some @$$ broke into my camero (at the time).They used a screwdriver under the lock on the door...toke it out and left a nise hole in thr door...and then they broke my center consloe just to get to my sony CD player ((( which was broke )))).<P>#^$* me off,...I fell for man.<P>After that I was thinking of setting up a tap for guys like that with a CD player with <BR>a stick on TNT in it.<P>But after thinking about it ....I do not fell like doing life.<P>Nice idea thou.....<P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||01-13-2001||04:15 PM||||cops tell me break ins, cars, homes, businesses are 75% of the time someone you know. Be on the lookout for any of your stuff. I had my best friend once go cruising years ago, i didnt know but he left the vent window unlatched. I went back home, he left and i went in the house. when I came back my tape deck was gone. the next week i saw it installed in his car........go figure.||||reg||1
