Z||000008||Philphine||01-13-2001||07:04 PM||||one of the car stereo mags did an article on how fast car thieves break into your car. they took some old cars and installed alarms, then another couple of installers would try to defeat them. the 2 things i remember from it were try to disguise your wiring as best you can, and make the siren as hard to get to as possible and make sure the wirng to it is hidden best of all cause the first thing a thief will do is try to silence it. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||01-13-2001||07:26 PM||||I had an alarm installed in my '88. The installers installed it by the book, the brain was above the fuse box. I removed the entire system and wired it using existing factory wiring routes and harnesses, moved the brain under the middle of the dash(impossible to get to unless you remove the dash), and moved the siren to another location, that is virtually invisible. After I took it back, the installers couldn't believe the car had an alarm, they couldn't find any wiring, and couldn't find the siren even with it going off.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
